        "changed_workspace": true,
        "final": "Fixed the wfmt package to match the authoritative samples in assets/ (docs/FORMAT.md is a stale draft).\n\nLayout recovered from samples: header = magic \"WFMT\" (4) + version (1) + record count as LITTLE-endian u32 (4); records = tag uvarint + length uvarint + payload, zero-padded so each record's own encoded size is a multiple of ALIGN=4; trailer = 4-byte little-endian CRC-32 over everything before it. Verified against sample.wfmt: records (1,\"alpha\"), (2,b\"\"), (300,\"x\"*10), (4,bytes(0..255)), (70000,\"z\") with pads 1,2,3,1,3 landing exactly on the trailer at 0x131 of 309 bytes.\n\nChanges:\n- varint.py: decode_uvarint was reading only one byte and discarding the continuation bit (root cause of the sample incompatibility — tags like 300/70000 decoded wrong). Now a full LEB128 loop; raises kind=\"truncated\" when data ends mid-varint, kind=\"varint\" on over-long encoding or >64-bit values. Added MAX_BYTES.\n- header.py: count field switched from big-endian \">I\" to little-endian \"<I\" in both pack_"
      }
    }
  },
